  </div>

  <div class="highlight-box highlight-box--teal">
    <p>
      <strong>Where ownership is real:</strong> a nutrition practice, a diagnostic collection centre or small lab, an agri-advisory or processing business, and a data service for labs each give you control of price, the chance to hire and repeat customers. Each needs the right registration, a niche and proof, so treat it as a later stage, not a first-year plan.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="honest-take">
    <p class="honest-take__label">Honest take</p>
    <p>
      Crowded courses stay on this list because many students need them. Microbiology, zoology, botany and biochemistry are easy to enter and slow to pay. They can work if you add a documented lab method, quality writing or data skill, and if you plan the MSc seat early.
    </p>
  </div>

  <h2 id="entry">Who can enter which BSc</h2>

  <p>
    Most of these courses take PCB. Maths is the usual lock, and it shuts data-led degrees. The entry route for each course is in its card above; always read the college page for the current year.
