            <td data-label="First sales skill to learn">{row.first}</td>
            <td data-label="One number to watch">{row.number}</td>
          </tr>
        ))}
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <div class="highlight-box highlight-box--teal">
    <p>
      Keep it basic. Say who you help and with what. Make one simple offer with a clear price. Show proof others can check. Follow up. Ask happy clients for a referral. In health and testing work, stay inside your registration and your council's rules, and never promise cures or guaranteed results.
    </p>
  </div>

  <h2 id="cost">College cost: the 10% rule and the debt check</h2>

  <p>
    Degrees matter for licensed careers, so a recognised and approved college is non-negotiable for nursing and allied health. But college is a small part of career success. Use roughly 10% of your total education budget as the starting figure for the degree, and treat anything above about 20% as a caution that needs course-specific evidence. These are planning heuristics, not laws.
  </p>

  <div class="table-wrap">
    <table class="paths-table">
      <thead>
        <tr><th>Total education budget</th><th>10% start</th><th>20% caution line</th><th>What fits</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        {costRows.map((row) => (
          <tr>
            <td data-label="Total education budget"><strong>{row.budget}</strong></td>
            <td data-label="10% start">{row.ten}</td>
            <td data-label="20% caution line">{row.twenty}</td>
            <td data-label="What fits">{row.fit}</td>
          </tr>
        ))}
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <ul>
    <li>Add every year: tuition, hostel, clinical and lab fees, exams and uniforms.</li>
    <li>Ask the college for last year's placement names, roles and pay, and how many students were eligible.</li>
    <li>If you could repay a loan only because you upskilled after the BSc, the loan was not the BSc's doing. Avoid debt unless the credential is legally needed.</li>
    <li>Spend above the benchmark only when the course gives a verified, hard-to-copy edge, such as clinical access, approvals, labs and real placement medians.</li>
  </ul>

